# What the language bar should say.
#
# GitHub's linguist counts every file it recognises, which puts TeX and Gherkin
# in the summary for a Python tool. The classifications below leave the bar
# reflecting what the repository actually is, without hiding anything: every
# file is still browsable, searchable and diffable.

# A generated LaTeX table, for pasting into a paper. Not source.
results/*.tex            linguist-documentation

# Sample and fixture specifications. They are input to the tool, not its
# implementation, and there are enough of them to skew the summary.
examples/*.feature       linguist-documentation
tests/fixtures/*.feature linguist-documentation

# Read by the evaluation harness through the Gherkin parser. Part of the study,
# not part of the tool.
evaluation/*.rb          linguist-vendored

# Measurements, not code.
results/*.csv            linguist-generated
corpus/MANIFEST.csv      linguist-generated

# Keep line endings sane for a tool that cares about them. .feature files are
# the artefact under test, so git must not rewrite their endings.
*.feature                -text
